{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians","id":1450560,"title":"Fun thought on Getimians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-01T03:40:34-07:00","id":1450560,"title":"Fun thought on Getimians","content":"I had a thought of something fun we could do with the concept behind Getimians. Since Getimians are characters who never existed, then...could some signature characters from previous editions be brought back as a Getimian? Could a form of Desus be brought into 3E as one? or maybe Lillun if she no longer exists (I've been assured we're not getting a hentai-monster-thing-loli this edition, but I don't know if that means the girl herself is entirely gone).<br /> <br /> Fun idea? or is this just my sleep deprivation talking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T03:47:47-07:00","id":1450561,"title":"","content":"If that's the sort of thing your group is fine with then have at, but most of those characters were removed for a reason and the game is better for their absence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T03:54:27-07:00","id":1450562,"title":"","content":"I am actually wondering if it is even possible for your Getimian to have been an Exalt at all in their &quot;previous&quot; life and how and if that would affect them.<br /> <br /> My players have never encountered Desus or Lillun, so bringing them back would mean nothing to them. What would be interesting, though, is to bring back their previous characters:<br /> <br /> &quot;You know that game where your old character toppled the Guild and accidentially burned Nexus to the ground? Yeah, that never happened in this game... but your new character has a clear memory of it happening.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":"to distinguish the characters that I were talking about. 06-01-2021, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:02:42-07:00","id":1450565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450562#post1450562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually wondering if it is even possible for your Getimian to have been an Exalt at all in their &quot;previous&quot; life and how and if that would affect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that it's not by default because if it was then the overwhelming majority of Getimian concepts we'd see would be former Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:08:05-07:00","id":1450568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450562#post1450562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually wondering if it is even possible for your Getimian to have been an Exalt at all in their &quot;previous&quot; life and how and if that would affect them.<br /> <br /> My players have never encountered Desus or Lillun, so bringing them back would mean nothing to them. What would be interesting, though, is to bring back their previous characters:<br /> <br /> &quot;You know that game where your character toppled the Guild and accidentially burned Nexus to the ground? Yeah, that never happened in this game... but your character has a clear memory of it happening.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>this is way better than my idea. then again seems mine was dumb anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:15:40-07:00","id":1450571,"title":"","content":"Mmm, well. Disregarding the extradiegetic issues, I see a few questions we'd have to think about.<br /> <br /> For one, the text in the preview is a bit dubious.<br /> <br /> The general summary of the Getimian Exalted put it like Getimians are &quot;plucked from an unrealised destiny&quot;, someone who could have been born into Creation, but weren't. There's a vision and idea of a world resting within them, but that's a world that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> However, later on in the Caste description, it does sound more like they were actually born into <i>one</i> Creation, just not <i>this</i> Creation, and that would imply they were taken from that world and put into ours.<br /> <br /> It's pretty unclear which one it is. Personally, I'm inclined to read it like the first one, because I don't have much interest in large-scale dimension shenanigans, and that would mean that Desus and Lillun could <i>not</i> be reborn as Getimians. After all, they already existed. The other reading would mean that, yeah, perhaps they could.<br /> <br /> Even with that reading, though, I'm wondering how much different a Getimian Desus or Lillun would have to be from the &quot;regular&quot; Desus or Lillun to count as having &quot;not existed&quot;. In my mind, they'd have to be almost entirely different people, and then what's the point of the exercise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":".  Formatting. 06-01-2021, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T05:04:17-07:00","id":1450575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450571#post1450571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm inclined to read it like the first one, because I don't have much interest in large-scale dimension shenanigans, and that would mean that Desus and Lillun could <i>not</i> be reborn as Getimians. After all, they already existed. The other reading would mean that, yeah, perhaps they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>A retcon or new edition effectively means that, <i>in-game</i>, the previous edition never happened.<br /> <br /> So both first edition and second edition never happened <i>in-game</i> even if the books were published in our world.<br /> <br /> I think, regardless of whether you choose option one or option two, Lillun could theoretically show up. She would still be the daughter of the Empress and whoever her father was, she would look as she did before bloating, and she would still be called Lillun, but her Fate would never be to be snatched away to Malfeas. Maybe she went on to become part of the Lesser Chamber of the Deliberative, where she succesfully argued for stricter laws against engaging with demons and became best friends with Nellens Cyan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T05:43:34-07:00","id":1450579,"title":"","content":"Lillun Exalting as a Getimian after escaping Hell and getting new life free from her torment is something she definitely deserves, IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T05:52:17-07:00","id":1450580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450575#post1450575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A retcon or new edition effectively means that, <i>in-game</i>, the previous edition never happened.<br /> <br /> So both first edition and second edition never happened <i>in-game</i> even if the books were published in our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah! No issues there. Your example of bringing in old characters from previous campaigns would also work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450575#post1450575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, regardless of whether you choose option one or option two, Lillun could theoretically show up. She would still be the daughter of the Empress and whoever her father was, she would look as she did before bloating, and she would still be called Lillun, but her Fate would never be to be snatched away to Malfeas. Maybe she went on to become part of the Lesser Chamber of the Deliberative, where she succesfully argued for stricter laws against engaging with demons and became best friends with Nellens Cyan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, not sure I agree that could happen in the first interpretation. After all, Lillun already existed, so her destiny wasn't unrealized and thus she couldn't be a Getimian. But I admit that this is all based on five lines of preview summary, so yeah, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T07:54:43-07:00","id":1450585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450580#post1450580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, Lillun already existed, so her destiny wasn't unrealized</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where we differ, because I would argue that from the point of view of third edition, she never existed. <br /> <br /> Just as Romeo and Juliet and Scooby Doo never existed in third edition, so is the case with Lillun. There is no Lillun in third edition.<br /> <br /> But we are just mincing words now, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T07:58:25-07:00","id":1450586,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, I see your point. But at that point, there's no imperative to make Lillun a Getimian. Since she's not in 3e, you could just add her like the Empress' daughter, just like you said above, and just like any other character introduced down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T08:42:54-07:00","id":1450588,"title":"","content":"That's fair.<br /> <br /> It is a wink and a nod. Nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:17:12-07:00","id":1450593,"title":"","content":"So... I've been trying to wrap my head around the concept of the Getimians. Would it be fair to think of them as the Isekai Exalted? That is, rather than thinking of them as never having existed before they were Exalted, could one instead think of them as merely never having existed <i>in Creation</i> before they were Exalted, and their Exaltation takes the form of pulling them out of some other reality and dumping them into Creation with powers? Those in Creation think of them as having come from non-existent realities; and since they can never go back, the question of whether or not their reality of origin actually exists is kind of moot. <br /> <br /> In particular, how similar does the Getimian's \u201cnative reality\u201d have to be to Creation? Could it, for instance, be as wildly different as the various Shards found in the 2e supplement Shards of the Exalted Dream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:42:13-07:00","id":1450597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450593#post1450593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I've been trying to wrap my head around the concept of the Getimians. Would it be fair to think of them as the Isekai Exalted? That is, rather than thinking of them as never having existed before they were Exalted, could one instead think of them as merely never having existed <i>in Creation</i> before they were Exalted, and their Exaltation takes the form of pulling them out of some other reality and dumping them into Creation with powers? Those in Creation think of them as having come from non-existent realities; and since they can never go back, the question of whether or not their reality of origin actually exists is kind of moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the intent; the writers don't want &quot;there is now a world missing the Getimian&quot;, even if they can never return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In particular, how similar does the Getimian's \u201cnative reality\u201d have to be to Creation? Could it, for instance, be as wildly different as the various Shards found in the 2e supplement Shards of the Exalted Dream? </div> </div> </div>Baseline is it diverges with whether the Getimian was ever born. It can extend further, as long as the result of the divergence is &quot;They were never born here&quot; - for example, if the Chanos Flicker in The Realm is a Getimian, then in the timeline he remembers House Chanos is an active thing, while in this Creation it's not, as it was struck from the imperial ledgers centuries ago.<br /> <br /> Course, the writers know full well individual tables are going to diverge further (or closer, having their counterpart die young in this timeline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:09:33-07:00","id":1450611,"title":"","content":"Fun thought, Get having alternate reality pasts means they have a decently viable excuse for joining any group that isn't likely to view them as KOS. (IE they were allies or friends in the original timeline to the Get's perspective.) So if you had a player debating whether they should be a lunar, a solar, abyssal, whatever exalt type. Then the Get is from the timeline where the character was the other major contender.<br /> &quot;Okay I know this plan, just turn into your mouse form. I can get you close enough to sneak in without an issue.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wrong me, not a Lunar bud.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 06-01-2021, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T18:21:01-07:00","id":1450654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450593#post1450593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I've been trying to wrap my head around the concept of the Getimians. Would it be fair to think of them as the Isekai Exalted? That is, rather than thinking of them as never having existed before they were Exalted, could one instead think of them as merely never having existed <i>in Creation</i> before they were Exalted, and their Exaltation takes the form of pulling them out of some other reality and dumping them into Creation with powers? Those in Creation think of them as having come from non-existent realities; and since they can never go back, the question of whether or not their reality of origin actually exists is kind of moot.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450597#post1450597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the intent; the writers don't want &quot;there is now a world missing the Getimian&quot;, even if they can never return.</div> </div> </div> </div>This issue bugs me, because Getimians have no in-character reason to believe that they <i>haven't</i> been isekai'd, as far as I'm aware. If they believe that they come from somewhere else, their top priority is (in many cases) going to be &quot;return home&quot;. But if they <i>do</i> have in-character reasons to know that they popped into existence yesterday with a full set of fabricated memories, then the pathos of dealing with those memories is flushed down the toilet, and so the only solution I can see is to just issue a metagame decree &quot;Getimians don't know they weren't real before, but they don't care about trying to go home because otherwise that would wrap the game around that objective&quot;, which feels incredibly unsatisfying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450593#post1450593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, how similar does the Getimian's \u201cnative reality\u201d have to be to Creation? Could it, for instance, be as wildly different as the various Shards found in the 2e supplement Shards of the Exalted Dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would rule that Getimians can only isekai between versions of a single Shards - Gunstar to Gunstar, Reach to Reach - unless I was planning to build a whole campaign around making exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T18:39:47-07:00","id":1450655,"title":"","content":"As an aside, does not Kagami - or one or more of the other souls of Szoreny - deal with alternate realities, people that were not, might have been and such?<br /> Could there be some connection or parallel or the Gentimians be chosen/Akuma of that particular Yozi?<br /> <br /> And if not, how does one see the difference from those &quot;akuma of who might have been&quot;?<br /> <br /> About &quot;isekaied&quot; individuals, one might point out they are overall closer to Abyssals or Liminals in being people who touched (or crossed) the edge of death, to then find themselves beginning again in different worlds. Sometimes in empowered versions of themselves, sometimes in whole new bodies/incarnations/lives.<br /> <br /> Just some spur-of-moment ramblings.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, isn't there in the Realm book a passing mention of what might be a rogue gentimian, a Dynast from house Ophrys that suddenly find itself in a Blessed Isle where it's <b>not</b> the prefect of its city but his house has been gone of the region for centuries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-01-2021, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T20:42:25-07:00","id":1450658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians#post1450560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought of something fun we could do with the concept behind Getimians. Since Getimians are characters who never existed, then...could some signature characters from previous editions be brought back as a Getimian? Could a form of Desus be brought into 3E as one? or maybe Lillun if she no longer exists (I've been assured we're not getting a hentai-monster-thing-loli this edition, but I don't know if that means the girl herself is entirely gone).<br /> <br /> Fun idea? or is this just my sleep deprivation talking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Getimians by default have to be mortal before they exalt. Even though getimians have never existed before they exalt, they still can't break the double exalt rule. That is they can not exalt after being another exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-01-2021, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T21:41:07-07:00","id":1450660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450658#post1450658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimians by default have to be mortal before they exalt. Even though getimians have never existed before they exalt, they still can't break the double exalt rule. That is they can not exalt after being another exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, if they WERE an Exalt, then it is unlikely that they would have been cut from reality in the first place. Certainly not impossible, but not probably either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T21:50:03-07:00","id":1450662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450655#post1450655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As an aside, isn't there in the Realm book a passing mention of what might be a rogue gentimian, a Dynast from house Ophrys that suddenly find itself in a Blessed Isle where it's <b>not</b> the prefect of its city but his house has been gone of the region for centuries?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're talking about a person from house Chanos in PG 111. Who is very confused about why his house gone and why house and why house Sesus has his stuff.<br /> <br /> Also funny enough he gets dreams from what I think is Thulio telling him what's going on in which case he promptly ignores as he is too busy stealing back his stuff.<br /> <br /> The devs from discord mentioned Thulio has some way to track down Gets and promptly comes himself, sends one of his agents -other gets probably- or as above talks to them in their dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-02-2021, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T22:55:48-07:00","id":1450665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450660#post1450660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention, if they WERE an Exalt, then it is unlikely that they would have been cut from reality in the first place. Certainly not impossible, but not probably either.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness if they're random glitches then a hero/heroine of a cut timeline would be still be cut regardless of exaltation status. House Vinderpan's champion who slew the Anathema known as Bull of the North at what would be called Futile Blood in the normal timeline is getting cut by virtue that Vinderpan's &quot;founder&quot; died in the academy over two centuries before that battle. All timelines springing from that and potential champions are consequently pruned regardless of exalt status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:45:58-07:00","id":1450730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anshu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450654#post1450654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they believe that they come from somewhere else, their top priority is (in many cases) going to be &quot;return home&quot;. But if they <i>do</i> have in-character reasons to know that they popped into existence yesterday with a full set of fabricated memories, then the pathos of dealing with those memories is flushed down the toilet,</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that's a very clinical way of approaching characterisation.<br /> <br /> Is this thread based on an awareness of who is responsible for the existence of the Getimians? Does (the yet released excerpt of) Essence mention that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:53:28-07:00","id":1450731,"title":"","content":"SLS's description from an RPG.net thread <br /> &quot;Wait, Getimians <i>were</i> world-changing mortals or <i>would have been</i> if they ever existed?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Would have been if they'd existed.<br /> <br /> My go-to example is, say, thirty-seven years ago, in Realm Year 731, the gods in the fate planning committees in the Bureau of Destiny were planning all the various destinies and future courses of history that they could plausibly plan (this is an important job, gotta keep the Loom running, and part of that is feeding it a month-to-month set of destinies to weave and ensuring the destinies you're telling it to weave are actually possible so it doesn't suffer a general protection fault or whatever happens if you tell the Loom to weave a fate in a way that isn't possible), and one of the courses of history they brainstorm up is one where, a year hence in RY 732, a girl is born who'll grow up to be a soldier and ascend to the rank of general in the army of some Southern state, and from there stage a coup and crown herself monarch, and from <i>there</i> prove to be an apt politician and weave together some sort of military alliance between major powers of the South that ultimately throws the yoke of the Realm out of that entire Direction. This is a thing that <i>could</i> happen. And the gods of the Bureau of Destiny look at that and go &quot;No, that'd fuck up all sorts of other things we want, and also reduce prayer quotas coming in from Immaculate populations, so we're not doing that.&quot; And so they don't enact that destiny, and there never is a girl born in RY 732 who's going to do those things. Her parents never meet because one of them is delayed half an hour going to the caravanserai they <i>could have</i> met at, because <i>that's</i> the fate heaven enacts instead.<br /> <br /> Three years ago in RY 765, this person, who could have been god-queen of the South if she'd been born, but wasn't born, Exalts as a Getimian. From her perspective she's lived the life she could have lived, in this divergent version of Creation in which she did all those things. She has the skills and memories that come with it. She remembers relationships and such. But from an external perspective she just suddenly popped into existence from nothing, courtesy of the Getimian Exaltation, at thirty-three years of age, remembering a bunch of stuff that never happened, having one-sided relationships with people whose lives maybe went entirely different directions because they never met her.<br /> <br /> Now it's RY 768 and she's been a Getimian for three years and you can play as her if you want.<br /> <br /> As far as Heaven is concerned this is disturbing on a number of levels, because now not only is she real, but also it implies all these destinies they dream up as hypotheticals and don't enact have some sort of moral weight? What the hell? Like there is a reason the world's creators looked at the Getimians when they were created and just noped right the fuck out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:54:00-07:00","id":1450732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450730#post1450730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though that's a very clinical way of approaching characterisation.<br /> <br /> Is this thread based on an awareness of who is responsible for the existence of the Getimians? Does (the yet released excerpt of) Essence mention that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is mentioned that Oramus and Sacheverell created and locked them up before they were imprisoned and diminished.<br /> <br /> it also states that they were released by one and called into service in a war against Heaven by the rogue Sidereal Rakan Thulio<br /> <br /> Just an excerpt from the essence manuscript and nothing extra from the discord or some other forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-02-2021, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T16:14:56-07:00","id":1450743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450730#post1450730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though that's a very clinical way of approaching characterisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's my autism, maybe it's my depression, but if I was told (and had some reason to believe) that I and my memories had been created <i>ex nihilo</i>, then I would feel I had no right to approach any of the real people who featured in those memories. It would be like me, a real person, going up to a performer of some kind and saying, &quot;I'm a big fan and I had a really vivid dream where you were my sibling/lover/parent/comrade&quot; \u2013 just totally inappropriate. So it would suck and I'd be sad, but then I'd just try to ignore those memories and find something else to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T16:22:23-07:00","id":1450744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anshu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450743#post1450743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's my autism, maybe it's my depression, but if I was told (and had some reason to believe) that I and my memories had been created <i>ex nihilo</i>, then I would feel I had no right to approach any of the real people who featured in those memories. It would be like me, a real person, going up to a performer of some kind and saying, &quot;I'm a big fan and I had a really vivid dream where you were my sibling/lover/parent/comrade&quot; \u2013 just totally inappropriate. So it would suck and I'd be sad, but then I'd just try to ignore those memories and find something else to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, what you just described, where people would go up to performers and relate to them in terms of those people's parasocial relationships with the performers' roles, happened <i>all the time</i> at the beginning of the era of mass media, and still continues today, although at this point we have years and years of socializing people not to do that. Getimians don't come from a time when everybody knows that it's absurd to go up to Lucille Ball and talk to her like she's really Lucy and she's your friend because you've hung out with her in your living room every afternoon for the last five years.<br /> <br /> You can play a Getimian who's more reserved or who's thought about the issue and come to the same conclusion you have here, but it's not an error of writing that that's not presented as the default.<br /> <br /> (That the Getimian grievance is arguably kinda illegitimate, depending on your frame of reference, and that they are a bunch of hyper-weirdos who make everyone uncomfortable with how they try to relate to the world and everyone in it, is deliberate. It is entirely possible that the &quot;good&quot; path for the Getimians is deciding that Rakan's agenda is bankrupt and he's a bad person for enabling their initial grievance in his attempts to serve his own agenda instead of helping them move past it and adapt better to the world as it is.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 06-02-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T17:25:15-07:00","id":1450751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450744#post1450744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, what you just described, where people would go up to performers and relate to them in terms of those people's parasocial relationships with the performers' roles, happened <i>all the time</i> at the beginning of the era of mass media, and still continues today</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you tell 'em Dudley!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T18:52:32-07:00","id":1450758,"title":"","content":"Harris knows what's up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:02:43-07:00","id":1450762,"title":"","content":"Having established the whole deal with Oramus, I would propose that Getimians might become aware of that Primordial's relationship with reality such that the distinction between actual fully realised world that they were plucked out of and having been given existence out of a preceding hypothetical state is somewhat fuzzy in the first place. One might even raise ontological questions about the ethics of dealing with a person who is technically newborn but the manner of their birth gives them a sense of connection to people and places that is genuine to them. I think the analogy to parasocial relationships falters in how those deal in a reality where such a thing is wholly based in delusion and crossing boundaries, and not quite engaged to the mythic aspect of things that relate to the cosmology in a particular way.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that anybody owes anything to Getimians*, just that the basis for their feelings and sense of self might not be written off entirely.<br /> <br /> Also, hey, get to act the part of George Bailey wandering frustrated through Pottersville.<br /> <br /> * Although I would not discount scenarios where allowing one into one's life turns out to actually be fulfilling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:14:29-07:00","id":1450765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450744#post1450744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, what you just described, where people would go up to performers and relate to them in terms of those people's parasocial relationships with the performers' roles, happened <i>all the time</i> at the beginning of the era of mass media, and still continues today, although at this point we have years and years of socializing people not to do that. Getimians don't come from a time when everybody knows that it's absurd to go up to Lucille Ball and talk to her like she's really Lucy and she's your friend because you've hung out with her in your living room every afternoon for the last five years.<br /> <br /> You can play a Getimian who's more reserved or who's thought about the issue and come to the same conclusion you have here, but it's not an error of writing that that's not presented as the default.<br /> <br /> (That the Getimian grievance is arguably kinda illegitimate, depending on your frame of reference, and that they are a bunch of hyper-weirdos who make everyone uncomfortable with how they try to relate to the world and everyone in it, is deliberate. It is entirely possible that the &quot;good&quot; path for the Getimians is deciding that Rakan's agenda is bankrupt and he's a bad person for enabling their initial grievance in his attempts to serve his own agenda instead of helping them move past it and adapt better to the world as it is.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am curious what percentage of Getimians settle on a conclusion along the lines of 'I was blissfully unaware of my nonexistence until you brought me into miserable existence in a strange alien world that doesn't match the memories in my head for use as fodder in your war' and try to punch Rakan Thulio in the face instead of blaming heaven for scrapping them in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:26:44-07:00","id":1450766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450765#post1450765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am curious what percentage of Getimians settle on a conclusion along the lines of 'I was blissfully unaware of my nonexistence until you brought me into miserable existence in a strange alien world that doesn't match the memories in my head for use as fodder in your war' and try to punch Rakan Thulio in the face instead of blaming heaven for scrapping them in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a Gemitian that works in heaven if I remember so there is a chance that some Gemitians would be alright with that sort of thing. I imagine especially when it comes to the Autumn caste that some of them find that their sacrifice or great work wasn't needed.<br /> <br /> For example, if say when they were mortal they managed to undo slavery somewhere through a bloody revolution only to exalt and find out that the bloody revolution or if they managed to protect their city from a massive fae invasion only to have them be stopped some Lunar or a legion of Dragon blooded would have mixed feelings instead of say anger.<br /> <br /> In regards to existential dread at realizing that you were a non-existent being until your very exaltation I honestly would imagine some not all but some would probably be happy with existing and would really not really care about the war between Thulio or heaven instead of going on their merry way curious to see what this new creation has, Its rare but its quite possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:56:31-07:00","id":1450772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450765#post1450765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'I was blissfully unaware of my nonexistence until you brought me into miserable existence in a strange alien world</div> </div> </div> </div>Who among us was not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You get some real life people who philosophise that their existence is an imposition that they did not consent to, but they seem to be a minority. I think at only 64 Getimians, the odds of catching such a persona are low.<br /> <br /> Arguably, the backstories that become Getimians are typically of the kind that view existence as innately worth having.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T01:35:43-07:00","id":1450790,"title":"","content":"Came to this thread to say &quot;High concept elevator pitch for Getimians: &quot;We remade 'Its A Wonderful Life' as a kung-fu epic starring Bond, and, plot twist, Clarence is a more ambiguous figure and enemy this time&quot;.&quot; Then got sad Levi made the reference first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Joking, lest I be interpreted seriously.)<br /> <br /> Find it interesting that the new Exalted, now we're seeing them, are profoundly more alienated from the world and themselves in some aspect than classic Exalted (who are pretty alienated themselves at times). More aspects of their powers or origin or identity seem to be distancing. Certainly more of like a more alienated WoD protagonist vibe about them? Open to seeing how that plays out. Exigents being the exception!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T05:42:48-07:00","id":1450803,"title":"","content":"Yeah...I'm still tempted to do a Getimian from the Gunstar shard, who was a Getimian in Gunstar, probably acting as a cut out to try and get the Incarna Exalts to assist against some new threat in exchange for some...delays to the Imperial fleet.<br /> I figure the more different from Creation their 'home' is, the more likely they are to reject both Thulio (who isekai kidnapped them) and the idea of accepting their new reality. Impossible quest to return to the nonexistant reality from whence they came seems like a solid starting motivation, all things considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T07:24:01-07:00","id":1450810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450662#post1450662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're talking about a person from house Chanos in PG 111. Who is very confused about why his house gone and why house and why house Sesus has his stuff.<br /> <br /> Also funny enough he gets dreams from what I think is Thulio telling him what's going on in which case he promptly ignores as he is too busy stealing back his stuff.<br /> <br /> The devs from discord mentioned Thulio has some way to track down Gets and promptly comes himself, sends one of his agents -other gets probably- or as above talks to them in their dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, that's the one, mixed up the defunct house names for some reason.<br /> <br /> And now i'm kind of imagining how would things be for a Gentimian that remembers being a Manosque or Iselsi version of Regent Fokuf.<br /> <br /> Or in a weirder vein, someone who remembers its house as the semi-defunct/hunted one, only to find it perfectly ok and fine in the Realm-as-is, for extra confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T07:44:32-07:00","id":1450814,"title":"","content":"I think it is interesting how one of the <b>Essence</b> devs (Monica, on the podcast <b>Systematic Understanding of Everything</b>) said that the Getimians skew antagonistic. <br /> <br /> I get that if you are a Sidereal because Getimians are antithetical to the job that you are trying to do, but I imagine that most Solars and Lunars (and Infernals and Abyssals too, to be fair) would be super open to working with a Getimian:<br /> <br /> &quot;So your resum\u00e9 says that you have first-hand experience smashing the patriarchy and seizing the means of production? Get in the warstrider. We've got stuff to do!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 06-03-2021, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:16:16-07:00","id":1450820,"title":"","content":"Regardless of patron origin I imagine that both infernal and gemitian go smashingly well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T09:39:49-07:00","id":1450836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450814#post1450814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is interesting how one of the <b>Essence</b> devs (Monica, on the podcast <b>Systematic Understanding of Everything</b>) said that the Getimians skew antagonistic.<br /> <br /> I get that if you are a Sidereal because Getimians are antithetical to the job that you are trying to do, but I imagine that most Solars and Lunars (and Infernals and Abyssals too, to be fair) would be super open to working with a Getimian:<br /> <br /> &quot;So your resum\u00e9 says that you have first-hand experience smashing the patriarchy and seizing the means of production? Get in the warstrider. We've got stuff to do!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that some of them might be a bit unhinged and hard to work with thanks to the trauma of their backstory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T12:12:44-07:00","id":1450862,"title":"","content":"I have a question regarding Gentimians. Are they all the result of destinies of people that never existed? Can there be a Gentimian that is the result of someone who exists but was &quot;cheated&quot; out of their glorious fate? It's just that there's so much potential drama in the second option.<br /> Just imagine an encounter between a Gentimian and the &quot;official&quot; version approved by heaven. Your Gentimian was a king, a general, or scholar with fame and fortune that made the world a better place in their reality, but then they found out that heaven decided &quot;Nah...forget about all that crap. Let's make this guy clean manure till 40 when he dies alone from an infection from cleaning manure&quot;<br /> Just imagine how angry you would be. And what about the &quot;official&quot; version? Would he hate you for showing just how much of a failure he is? Would he become your ally seeking revenge against heaven? Perhaps you inspire him to become something better now that he knows for a fact that the possibility exists and change his fate...<br /> I'm just throwing ideas out there. I thought it would be cool, but it doesn't matter if it's not an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T12:49:10-07:00","id":1450868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450862#post1450862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question regarding Gentimians. Are they all the result of destinies of people that never existed? Can there be a Gentimian that is the result of someone who exists but was &quot;cheated&quot; out of their glorious fate? It's just that there's so much potential drama in the second option.<br /> Just imagine an encounter between a Gentimian and the &quot;official&quot; version approved by heaven. Your Gentimian was a king, a general, or scholar with fame and fortune that made the world a better place in their reality, but then they found out that heaven decided &quot;Nah...forget about all that crap. Let's make this guy clean manure till 40 when he dies alone from an infection from cleaning manure&quot;<br /> Just imagine how angry you would be. And what about the &quot;official&quot; version? Would he hate you for showing just how much of a failure he is? Would he become your ally seeking revenge against heaven? Perhaps you inspire him to become something better now that he knows for a fact that the possibility exists and change his fate...<br /> I'm just throwing ideas out there. I thought it would be cool, but it doesn't matter if it's not an option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All Gemitians are people who were destinies that were cut by heaven and reduced to nonexistance.<br /> <br /> Mind you this doesn't stop you from doing that at your table creating a character that exists but was cheated which is kinda similar to Nocturnals when I think about it. The devs have gone on record to do whatever you desire on your table such as having your character a dragon blooded master Sidereal Martial arts as it doesn't really break and would honestly make something interesting for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T12:59:01-07:00","id":1450870,"title":"","content":"I mean if you were really concerned with staying within a strict reading of canon but still wanted to play that character, you could make a Getimian who was one of a pair of identical twins, and in the Getimian's history he survived and his brother died in childbirth and he did great things, but in the real history he died in childbirth and his brother survived and the real brother's life went a completely different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:26:13-07:00","id":1450875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450814#post1450814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is interesting how one of the <b>Essence</b> devs (Monica, on the podcast <b>Systematic Understanding of Everything</b>) said that the Getimians skew antagonistic.<br /> <br /> I get that if you are a Sidereal because Getimians are antithetical to the job that you are trying to do, but I imagine that most Solars and Lunars (and Infernals and Abyssals too, to be fair) would be super open to working with a Getimian:<br /> <br /> &quot;So your resum\u00e9 says that you have first-hand experience smashing the patriarchy and seizing the means of production? Get in the warstrider. We've got stuff to do!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it would depend on the Get and their history, but I imagine they probably have a tendency to lean antagonistic towards someone/something in the main timeline. Example a Get who's the scion of some Great House that never was in history proper due to their slot being occupied by House Tepet will probably be cheesed at Tepet for usurping, and probably screwing up, what the Get believes is rightfully they're house's. Heck any Get who was a devout follower of the Immaculate Order is probably still antagonistic towards Solars and Lunars (assuming those were default anathema in their timeline) by virtue of that being a constant. Heck they might cling to it more because its familiar to them. Also doesn't hurt if they have a grudge against the group for stuff that happened in their timeline.<br /> <br /> An amusing one would be a Get who views proper history as better than their own timeline. Not perfect, obviously, not like &quot;Why would I want to change any of this?&quot; but more of, &quot;I mean I'm not keen on the slave trade and the bandits, and the people who want me dead for existing -that part reminds me of home- but I do have to admit a fondness for not being swarmed by the undead, the machine men, and those scorpion gator hordes on a day to day basis.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:40:02-07:00","id":1450877,"title":"","content":"You know, all of this talk about Getimians made me remember this quote by Richard Dawkins (as it was quoted in Greatest Show On Earth by Nightwish):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;We are going to die, and that makes us the lucky ones</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Most people are never going to die because they are never going to be born</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The potential people who could have been here in my place</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">But who will in fact never see the light of day outnumber the sand grains of Sahara</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Certainly those unborn ghosts include greater poets than Keats, scientists greater than Newton</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We know this because the set of possible people allowed by our DNA</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So massively exceeds the set of actual people</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the teeth of those stupefying odds it is you and I, in our ordinariness, that are here</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We privileged few, who won the lottery of birth against all odds</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">How dare we whine at our inevitable return to that prior state</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">From which the vast majority have never stirred?&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> I must admit that before connecting those dots I had second thoughts about the Getimians- but now that I think of it in that respect, that not only are they those people who were meant to be heroes yet removed from existence, but that from the endless destinies only a few scattered fates were chosen, and from those fates only those specific unreal people were deemed heroic enough to be born into a Creation which refused to allow them to exist- well, how amazing is that?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T16:25:04-07:00","id":1450889,"title":"","content":"At the same time, the Getimians are REAL now, from their perspective at least. I can see them go full Pinocchio and try to convince everyone around them of this. I can see them spiral out of control based on the assertions that they aren't. They could be delusional and try to &quot;return Creation back to the way it was/should be&quot;, which is very antagonistic. They could be furious that their hard work has been undone, so they set about redoing their great deeds again; having to overthrow the tyranical government they have already replaced seems like a fun idea.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is just where they start. Stay long enough in 'normal' Creation and they might start to like it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-10-2021, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:22:08-07:00","id":1450925,"title":"","content":"I dont know somehow the Getiman remind me a bit of the changelings.<br /> <br /> Also i wonder how they are anchored in their new (can i say new if the old reality never existed?) reality. I think it would be funny if they hijacked the Body of their existing version.<br /> I mean how else do you anchor someone from an non-existing reality in the existing one without having a double running around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:43:31-07:00","id":1450928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mugbearer23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450925#post1450925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know somehow the Getiman remind me a bit of the changelings.<br /> <br /> Also i wonder how they are anchored in their new (can i say new if the old reality never existed?) reality. I think it would be funny if they hijacked the Body of their existing version.<br /> I mean how else do you anchor someone from an non-existing reality in the existing one without having a double running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>...'Cause they don't usually have a counterpart running around in the first place? Default assumption is that in mainline Creation the Getimian was never born - the divergence point can be further back, but ultimately it ends with the Getimian never being born.<br /> <br /> I'd chalk it up to the Exaltation, myself. If the Liminal Exaltation can basically create a new (un)life using a corpse, the Getimian Exaltation can anchor a discarded destiny in mainline Creation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:56:20-07:00","id":1450930,"title":"","content":"Hm yeah that works to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T06:39:15-07:00","id":1451048,"title":"","content":"Hum, do Getimians Exaltation reincarnate? The Chosen get their aborted-history circa Creation in 2nd age, instead of Creation in Primordial Times, so I guess the process is made to get new Chosen, so it seems to be so.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if the Chosen got to be really out-there early divergence places, they could very different and alien views! What if the Primordials won, they could get on with the Infernals like brothers! Or really, really not, depending on how bad it would be. <br /> <br /> And if the parallel world was a recent branch and consistent, not a complete fabrication, a Getimian could have gotten information that was useful to the world. Maybe she was a mortal Dynast who saw the Realm civil war starting early, and got to know who first hand who were the traitors from each house, and who were the spies from outside? Now she gets to redo it properly, hidden while saving her House!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T11:40:29-07:00","id":1451069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1450868#post1450868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> All Gemitians are people who were destinies that were cut by heaven and reduced to nonexistance.<br /> <br /> Mind you this doesn't stop you from doing that at your table creating a character that exists but was cheated which is kinda similar to Nocturnals when I think about it. The devs have gone on record to do whatever you desire on your table such as having your character a dragon blooded master Sidereal Martial arts as it doesn't really break and would honestly make something interesting for your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually having a go at porting the Nocturnals into Exalted Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T15:25:02-07:00","id":1451080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451069#post1451069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually having a go at porting the Nocturnals into Exalted Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've also found myself starting to ponder about doing an Essence update to them after reading the previews. I still try to define their identity in relation to the other new Exalts (mostly the Getimians, but also the Hearteaters and the Umbrals to some degree), so I need to refine them a bit before I'll actually do such an update. I would still be very interested in seeing your version, however!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T16:30:09-07:00","id":1451081,"title":"","content":"I do wonder what prompted their caste names, since those aren't the five seasons in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T17:07:57-07:00","id":1451084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451081#post1451081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder what prompted their caste names, since those aren't the five seasons in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually are. They even were back in First Edition (which is why there can be a Deathlord called the Mask of Winters), even if that one confusingly also used the term season to describe the divisions in the Realm calendar named for the elements. Third Edition clarifies a bit by having the periods of climate shift be called seasons and the divisions of the calendar be called cycles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T19:16:42-07:00","id":1451095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451069#post1451069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually having a go at porting the Nocturnals into Exalted Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking forward to seeing what you come up with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T20:44:15-07:00","id":1451105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451084#post1451084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They actually are. They even were back in First Edition (which is why there can be a Deathlord called the Mask of Winters), even if that one confusingly also used the term season to describe the divisions in the Realm calendar named for the elements. Third Edition clarifies a bit by having the periods of climate shift be called seasons and the divisions of the calendar be called cycles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I keep forgetting that. Thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:24:48-07:00","id":1451110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451080#post1451080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I've also found myself starting to ponder about doing an Essence update to them after reading the previews. I still try to define their identity in relation to the other new Exalts (mostly the Getimians, but also the Hearteaters and the Umbrals to some degree), so I need to refine them a bit before I'll actually do such an update. I would still be very interested in seeing your version, however!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm being fairly non-committal towards their lore, my personal preference for Nox in 3rd edition is the Incarna that Never Was that's <i>somehow</i> trying to worm his way into existence and has created Exalts capable of bringing non-existent things into reality to help with that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451095#post1451095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to seeing what you come up with!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/viewtopic.php?p=1603#p1603\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> what I've got so far. I ultimately intend to cross-post but there's still Fluctuations, Iconic powers and of course Limit Break to sort out first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T22:51:17-07:00","id":1451117,"title":"","content":"I actually had a thought regarding Getimians: Is it possible for them to emerge from discarded destinies, regardless of whether Heaven <i>wanted</i> them discarded or not? I'm asking because of how prior editions talked about Essence use messing with how Destiny is supposed to go.<br /> <br /> Here's a scenario: A Getimian and a Chosen of Serenity have a talk. The Getimian is fairly belligerent, upset that due to her parent's never meeting in this world, she was never born here, and thus wasn't able to raise the family business to the mercantile empire it should have been. Having spoken (but not joined up with) Thulio before, she's aware that Heaven is generally responsible for discarded destinies, hence her situation. The Sidereal however clarifies: The Get's parents <i>were</i> supposed to get together, that was actually the original plan. However, due to the actions of an Anathema (presumably Lunar), the Get's father was seduced away, leaving the family business to rot and never meeting the Get's mother. While the Bureau of Destiny <i>could</i> have forced the issue, to do so would require active (and dangerous) Sidereal involvement, possibly risking an agent dying to a frenzied Lunar's claws. So, they let the situation be and focused on cleaning up the area. Thus, the Get's parents never met and had a child (her), the family business died on the vine and was never able to grow, and the Sidereals lost a prime &quot;investment&quot; for the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T20:45:17-07:00","id":1451412,"title":"","content":"Finally getting some details about the Getimians has me thinking back to those three sample characters we heard about back in the day - so long, I can't even find where they first posted, just <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/87238-what-do-we-know-about-rakan-thulio?p=87283#post87283\">seven years</a> worth of quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Minuend used to be the feared and worshiped sorcerer-queen of a wealthy, upstart kingdom in the deep South, until she woke up one day and wasn't. She aims to reclaim what was taken from her, and to punish those responsible.<br /> <br /> An-Ko-Shi has dedicated his fists to justice. He particularly focuses on delivering punishment to the wicked in absence of a derelict Heaven. He eagerly builds his strength for the day when he can cast down Fakharu, the corrupt censor of the West.<br /> <br /> Apkallu was a gambler who lost and won his freedom, won and lost a fortune, then gained Exaltation. Despite his roguish background, he holds the preservation of Creation against the vices of the mighty as his most pressing concern, and so has forsaken Rakan Thulio's dream. He works as a special consultant for the Bureau of Destiny. </div> </div> </div>In those long years of periodically seeing this, it oddly never occurred to me that Minuend's situation was a defining through-line of the splat. Hindsight rerolls 1s until they cease to appear, I suppose.<br /> <br /> With what we've learned...<br /> <br /> Minuend, as a Sorceress, sounds like a Winter (though she might be a Summer). It's obviously vague, but she could indicate a less-sympathetic version of Getimians: they're repeatedly called &quot;heroes&quot; of their timelines, but I don't see any indication that Minuend's deeds (or those of Getimians as a whole) were necessarily righteous. Heaven could avert the rise of a terrible tyrant... who suddenly shows up, wanting to take back all their old power and more. I wonder how some of the other Getimians would respond to that? It might raise some friction with the likes of...<br /> <br /> An-Ko-Shi is a classic Heroic Warrior, so probably a Spring. I wonder what his old timeline was like? There's interesting possibilities: maybe the cut Destiny wasn't meant to be &quot;about&quot; him, but was instead an experiment in casting down Fakharu, which allowed a good (and, presumably, pretty badass) life for An himself, but caused larger problems (as far as Heaven is concerned, anyway), so now he assumes he's in the Dark Timeline where Fakharu got to keep messing stuff up. At the opposite extreme, it might be pretty cool if he somehow became an agent of Heaven (if you want to bend Getimian lore a little, maybe even a God, Talespinner style), and had cleaned house in the past. There's something appealing about a Getimian with firsthand knowledge of Yu-Shan's inner workings, now using those skills to infiltrate and oppose the Sidereals' stronghold... honestly, maybe even moreso if it's someone who sounds like they're not really cut out for skulduggery. In a way, that would make for the exact opposite of...<br /> <br /> Apkallu isn't just the clincher that these guys don't go for easy-to-remember names. (Really, not even a single Broken Thread or Seven Deadly Honors. Such defiance of Creation's order.) No, Apkallu is also the concept here that I like the least. Personally, I feel like Getimians who walked away from Thulio, and maybe even provided some covert aid to Heaven, are fine, but if one of them is actually going to work directly with the Bureau of Destiny, that should happen <i>during</i> play, not before. A big part of what makes Getimians scary is how strange and unknown their powers are, so I wouldn't give the Sidereals a chance to study those in a safe setting unless and until the PCs make that happen. Still, the indications of his past are intriguing - I've seen people musing on the idea of Getimians who didn't really like their original version of Creation, and here we seem to have one that at least views his as a mixed bag - and that does seem to have made him less receptive to Thulio's sales pitch. I'd speculate that Apkallu is a Summer (there isn't much to go on, but &quot;iconoclast who upends order&quot; seems as good a summation as any), and hope he still breaks out the old trickster Archetype habits by using Impossible Conquest Authority to make minor Spirits tell their bosses exactly what they think of them.<br /> <br /> I was really only interested in An-Ko-Shi before Essence (that &quot;heroic antagonist&quot; energy), but having more context clearly gives me several potentially-intriguing takes on each brief sketch, which (like this thread itself) probably speaks well for the versatility of the new Exalts' themes... not bad, for something so odd and specific that those &quot;in the know&quot; famously struggled to come up with any analogues from other media!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T23:43:31-07:00","id":1451417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451412#post1451412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was really only interested in An-Ko-Shi before Essence (that &quot;heroic antagonist&quot; energy), but having more context clearly gives me several potentially-intriguing takes on each brief sketch, which (like this thread itself) probably speaks well for the versatility of the new Exalts' themes... not bad, for something so odd and specific that those &quot;in the know&quot; famously struggled to come up with any analogues from other media!</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest pop culture analogue I can think of is when David Tennant starts ranting about &quot;the Could Have Been King and his army of Meanwhiles and Never-Weres&quot; on Doctor Who. The show never went into any more detail about them, but the names are suggestive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T07:12:57-07:00","id":1451440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451417#post1451417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest pop culture analogue I can think of is when David Tennant starts ranting about &quot;the Could Have Been King and his army of Meanwhiles and Never-Weres&quot; on Doctor Who. The show never went into any more detail about them, but the names are suggestive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, now that we have a more complete picture, I think the mistake is looking for a specific character. Getimians exist in the form of a classic stock <i>situation</i>:<ul><li>Wolverine in House of M.</li> <li>Marty McFly in Back To The Future 2.</li> <li>Nodwick in A World Without Piffany.</li> <li>Bishop in the Age of Apocalypse.</li> <li>Captain Kirk in Mirror, Mirror.</li> <li>George Bailey seeing the world where he was never born.</li> </ul><br /> You know, the one character who remembers a better world than the awful version which everyone around them accepts, and is constantly freaking out at everyday stuff for being upsetting and wrong. Of course, those examples all share one key difference from the Getimian situation: the point of each and every story is to fix the world back to what the character remembers.<br /> <br /> Getimians don't get that. They're stuck in the wrong world forever. That's incredibly tragic, but also it may provide the best context for the idea of them being fundamentally antagonistic: deep down, I think that most Getimians would choose the annihilation of every being in Creation to bring back &quot;their&quot; version of it. On a philosophical level, the fact that the Getimian exists at all seems to imply that this is not an inherently greater crime than the simple existence of fate itself, which is maaaaybe doing that to countless &quot;potential destiny&quot; people all the time. On a practical level, if you live in this version of Creation, it's virtually indistinguishable from the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> ...I really like all the possibilities of this new splat, is I guess what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> (If you want to keep New Who in there, I'd actually lean into The Doctor in The Long Game and Bad Wolf, when he keeps going on about how this supposed to be &quot;the fourth great and bountiful human empire,&quot; much to everybody's confusion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T08:15:17-07:00","id":1451443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451440#post1451440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, now that we have a more complete picture, I think the mistake is looking for a specific character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The four Castes <i>were</i> each apparently inspired by a character from Morrowind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:43:22-07:00","id":1451492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451440#post1451440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the one character who remembers a better world than the awful version which everyone around them accepts, and is constantly freaking out at everyday stuff for being upsetting and wrong. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works. I think that the &quot;time traveller from bad future&quot; concept - Terminator, 12 Monkeys, Days of Future Past - can also be an inspiration. Not that they're actually time travellers, but their version of Creation could easily be worse than the real one, and they could be motivated to prevent that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T07:33:40-07:00","id":1451538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451492#post1451492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that works. I think that the &quot;time traveller from bad future&quot; concept - Terminator, 12 Monkeys, Days of Future Past - can also be an inspiration. Not that they're actually time travellers, but their version of Creation could easily be worse than the real one, and they could be motivated to prevent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given several X-men characters someone upthread listed as an example, I can also think of the first appearances of Rachel Summers in the X-men comics here. Even if you have a Gentimian who fixed a world that had gotten awful for them and their loved ones, them discovering that 'prime' Creation never hit the disaster that they ended up fixing in divergent-Creation (or that it was delayed and they could prevent it here), you can still get the personal drama of 'I see people I care about who are alive that I saw die, but I can't get those relationships back because to these people, I never existed, I'm just this weirdo that claims to know them, and maybe some of them still died in this timeline, but earlier'. <br /> <br /> So you still hit the core element of a person out of place, even if their motivation is 'let's do this better here, so the world doesn't need saving'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24133-stareyes","name":"Stareyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T12:19:42-07:00","id":1451560,"title":"","content":"You know, it just occurred to me that considering how Getimians are formed, the Great Prophecy seems like a powerful catalyst which could cause many Getimians to rise from it. How would a Getimian from a world where the Sidereals tried to support the Solars and succeed react when they enter such a diminished Creation where the Solars are branded as Anathema react? Or a Getimian rising from the future where they failed, bringing an eternal age of darkness? Or perhaps the one where they did nothing, allowing the world to rot as a lone heroic soul managed to escape the decaying universe? The first would almost certainly see the Sidereals and the Dragon Blooded as corrupted rule and support Rakan Thulio's war against Heaven, while the second and the third may actually support the Sidereals for &quot;doing the right choice&quot;- or perhaps see them as untrustworthy, considering that they know that they can do mistakes. And how the Sidereals themselves would react to those Getimian who stand as an eternal reminder for the future which they did not choose, which could be both better and worse then the path which was decided? Worse, how will they react to the fact that simply by consulting Fate in order to make a choice instead of doing it by their own, they have caused the creation of such tormented souls- or ones which came from a future brighter than they could ever imagine?<br /> <br /> I think it could make some very cool character concepts, personally, and I do wonder if we will see some example characters for those discarded futures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T12:28:58-07:00","id":1451562,"title":"","content":"Are such far back &quot;divergence points&quot; canonically allowed? (If so then maybe another option is Bonk the Cave-Getimian wondering where all the Dragon Kings got to?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T12:34:06-07:00","id":1451563,"title":"","content":"It could be a Getimian which is found in the corresponding &quot;present&quot; for that timeline- like a golden age of the Solars as guided by the Sidereals, and how it would look like &quot;right now&quot;, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T12:36:33-07:00","id":1451564,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that, canonically, the divergence point is the conception, birth, and/or not immediately dying to SIDS of the Getimian themself. The Essence writers have said that if you want to do things differently at your own table, nothing breaks (and from the looks of threads like this one, most people immediately go to wildly different Creations), but that seem to be the intention.<br /> <br /> That's kind of pieced together from multiple statements, though, so if anyone has anything more directly, please do correct me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T13:46:00-07:00","id":1451570,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to play the paradoxical Getimian who if he\u2019s been alive would have prevented the release and Exaltation of the Getimians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T13:52:14-07:00","id":1451572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450560-fun-thought-on-getimians?p=1451564#post1451564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that, canonically, the divergence point is the conception, birth, and/or not immediately dying to SIDS of the Getimian themself. The Essence writers have said that if you want to do things differently at your own table, nothing breaks (and from the looks of threads like this one, most people immediately go to wildly different Creations), but that seem to be the intention.<br /> <br /> That's kind of pieced together from multiple statements, though, so if anyone has anything more directly, please do correct me!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd point to the Getimian version of the Chanos Flicker in <i>The Realm</i>, whose divergence point - whether House Chanos gets removed from the imperial ledgers - is several centuries back. The writers have said an origin that far back is on the far end of the curve, but it is still on the curve.<br /> <br /> Basically, what matters is that the Getimian wasn't born in Creation-that-is, even if that wasn't the direct result of the destiny Heaven chose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}